from pathlib import Path
import html,json
root=Path('scratch')
records=json.loads((root/'qa-open-transcript.json').read_text())
before=json.loads((root/'qa-open-before-fix.json').read_text())
def esc(x):return html.escape(str(x))
def transcript(r):
    text=r.get('stdout','')+r.get('stderr','')
    return f'<details><summary><code>{esc(r["command"])}</code> <span>exit {r["code"]}</span></summary><pre>{esc(text)}</pre></details>'
scenarios=[
('First arrival; focus absent','Fresh Git repository, local identity, private HOME/LF_HOME and provider directories. Create a real Task, start the built server, then lf open --focus.','Failed with “Not open”; session list remained empty. Conflicting --here --tab flags were rejected.'),
('Plain terminal','lf open --tab --host terminal','Failed with a command to run manually using --here. No fallback host launched.'),
('Repository conversation in Rex','Prepare the repository Session; lf open --tab --host rex --server <private socket>.','One Conversation block, usable receipt, real Codex sign-in screen. No workspace/workflow substitution.'),
('Already open and unfocusable view','Repeat the repository opening, then --focus.','Repeat returned elsewhere with the original Session and block IDs. Focus returned a failure explaining that no capable Rex display client existed; it created no replacement.'),
('Direct Task opening inside Rex','Create one real Rex window executing lf open --task <task>, with no mode flag.','Codex appeared in that same block. Task status showed no Graph; primary Session belonged to the Task. No extra conversation window appeared.'),
('Agent own-Session and sibling defaults','Use a private provider’s recorded caller provenance as LF_AGENT_CALLER; open its own Session, then a new Wave.','Own-Session open returned elsewhere. --here failed with the interactive-terminal instruction. Wave opening created exactly one sibling Conversation block in the same Rex container. This exercised real CLI routing with a constructed agent environment; no authenticated tool call ran.'),
('Closed history, startup failure, retry','Ctrl+C in the repository Codex terminal; confirm closed. Put invalid TOML in the private provider config and open the same Session. Restore the file and repeat the exact command.','Before the fix, retry failed with “No such file or directory (os error 2)”. After the fix, the retained failure tab showed the config error, retry returned usable, and a delayed capture showed the sign-in screen. Session card was active and transition resumed the same provider thread.'),
('Workspace overview','lf workspace --wave reports --host rex --server <private socket>; compare Session inventories before and after.','Overview completed; the set of Session IDs was unchanged.'),
('Concurrent Herdr opening and focus','Create and prepare another real Task. Send two simultaneous --tab --host herdr opens to a private Herdr server, then --focus.','One usable result and one elsewhere result; pane inventory contained one Conversation pane. Focus returned focused. Immediate pane capture was empty, so this establishes attachment and host selection, not visible Herdr rendering.'),
('Returning release state','Prepare a repository Session with the installed release in a second private Machine; repeat preparation with the branch binary.','Session identity remained unchanged. This checks preparation across versions, not a full authenticated history upgrade.'),
('Desktop without a display','Build the app and run affected production model/view checks with WindowServer denied.','Five tests in three suites passed, including eight composed-opening cases. Loading/unavailable/empty/selected Work, native readiness, failed-open retry and elsewhere handling were exercised. No live Desktop window was opened.'),
('Cleanup','Stop native and Loopflow servers, private recorded owners and their descendants; reap child processes.','No remaining process command named any private QA root. No service was installed, no native app bundle launched, and no personal Session was attached.')]
sections=''.join(f'<tr><th>{esc(a)}</th><td>{esc(b)}</td><td>{esc(c)}</td></tr>' for a,b,c in scenarios)
selected=[r for r in records if r.get('command','').startswith(('lf open','lf workspace','lf session card')) or 'block capture' in r.get('command','') or 'pane list' in r.get('command','')]
failures=[r for r in before if r.get('command','').startswith('lf open --session') and 'No such file or directory' in r.get('stdout','')]
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>LOO-825 · Opening QA</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1120px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#25302d;background:#f5f4ef}h1{font-size:40px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin-bottom:8px}h2{margin-top:40px}p{max-width:850px}.label{color:#426456;font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px}.result{border-left:4px solid #387255;padding:12px 20px;background:#e7eee7}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:15px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #cfd5cb}th{width:19%}td{width:40%}code,pre{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:12px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;padding:16px;background:#e7e8e1}details{border-bottom:1px solid #ccd3c9;padding:10px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary span{color:#657569}a{color:#185f4d}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{background:#161c19;color:#dce5dc}.result,pre{background:#233029}a{color:#a5d8bf}th,td,details{border-color:#3c4b40}.label{color:#a5bfb0}}
</style><p class="label">LOO-825 · QA · 10 November 2026</p><h1>Retry reaches the conversation</h1>
<p class="result">Found and fixed a startup-recovery defect. A failed provider reservation could retain a transport ID after its socket was removed. Opening now treats that retired transport as having no attached view and lets the existing Session resolver continue. The same real command now reattaches after correcting the provider config.</p>
<p>Branch base for this run: <code>1b8c46d8f</code>, plus the repair in <code>open.rs</code> and the expanded failure/retry regression. All writes used disposable repositories and Machine/provider homes under <code>/tmp/lf-qa-open-*</code>. Native terminals ran actual Codex and stopped at sign-in.</p>
<h2>What was exercised</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Action</th><th>Observed result</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+sections+'''</tbody></table>
<h2>The repair</h2><p><code>conversation_view</code> previously propagated a missing socket as a fatal opening error. It now uses the transport’s existing <code>leaving</code> reading when an attachment probe fails. Other probe errors remain errors, with context. This changes no input takeover or provider-replacement policy. The regression covers a reserved provider with a retired transport, absent focus, and successful same-Session retry.</p>
<h2>Checks</h2><ul><li><code>cargo build -p loopflow --bin lf</code> — passed; real walkthrough rerun after rebuilding the repair.</li><li><code>cargo test -p loopflow --test integration failed_attachment_returns_failure_and_the_same_command_can_retry</code> — passed; <a href="qa-regression.log">log</a>.</li><li><code>scripts/test_desktop.sh --filter 'DesktopHeadlessTests/workStates|conversationAttachment|composedOpeningWaitsForNativeSessionAndComparison|ServerConnectionTests/openingWaitsForNativeReadinessAndRecoversInPlace'</code> — five tests passed; <a href="qa-desktop.log">log</a>. Run before the Rust-only repair.</li><li><code>cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings</code> — passed; <a href="qa-clippy.log">log</a>.</li><li><code>cargo fmt --check</code> and <code>git diff --check</code> — passed.</li></ul>
<h2>Failure before the repair</h2>'''+''.join(transcript(r) for r in failures)+'''<h2>Final walkthrough transcripts</h2><p>Expandable CLI results and real terminal captures. <a href="qa-open-transcript.json">Complete final transcript</a> · <a href="qa-open-before-fix.json">Before-fix transcript</a> · <a href="qa_open.py">Walkthrough driver</a>.</p>'''+''.join(transcript(r) for r in selected)+'''
<h2>What works now; what remains unchecked</h2><p>The exercised CLI/native paths attach to the requested conversation, keep existing input in place, reject unsupported modes, and recover after the corrected startup error. No unresolved defect was observed in those paths.</p><ul><li>Authenticated replies, real provider tool calls and prompt-history replay were not exercised: the private provider home has no credentials. Thread identity was checked, but no conversational content was sent.</li><li>No mounted Desktop window, Rex display-client focus, or visible Herdr TUI was inspected. Desktop coverage here is automated and headless; Herdr focus is confirmed by its real server.</li><li>A live delayed-readiness/acknowledgement-timeout scenario, remote Machine ownership and workspace partial-failure rendering were not repeated in this walkthrough. Earlier focused tests remain recorded in the design; they do not establish live acceptance.</li><li>Gate still owns the broader affected suites and Xcode fallback build. This run does not diagnose the earlier parallel host-request timeouts.</li></ul><p>Native launch and failure-recovery instructions were added to <code>.lf/skills/qa.md</code>. All private servers and recorded children were stopped. No PR publication, merge or Graph-step selection was performed.</p></html>'''
(root/'qa.html').write_text(page)
